@startuml SSD_UC005_Backward_On_Three_Side_Obstacle_Without_Right_Sensor
hide footbox
title SSD - UC-005 Move Backward After Three-Side Obstacle Detection - Without Right Sensor

actor "Sensor Input" as Sensor
participant "RVC SW Controller" as System
actor "Driving Device" as Drive

alt backward available
    note right of System: UC-003 confirmed front, left,\nand previous right direction are blocked.
    Sensor -> System: reportBackObstacleState(backObstacleDetected=false)
    activate System
    System -> Drive: stop()
    System -> Drive: moveBackward()

    alt left available after backward movement
        Sensor -> System: reportLeftObstacleState(leftObstacleDetected=false)
        note right of System: Continue with UC-003;\nleft avoidance is selected first.
    else left blocked and previous right direction open after probe
        Sensor -> System: reportLeftObstacleState(leftObstacleDetected=true)
        System -> Drive: turnRight90()
        Sensor -> System: reportFrontObstacleState(frontObstacleDetected=false)
        note right of System: Use current heading as right avoidance;\ncontinue with UC-004.
    else left blocked and previous right direction still blocked
        Sensor -> System: reportLeftObstacleState(leftObstacleDetected=true)
        System -> Drive: turnRight90()
        Sensor -> System: reportFrontObstacleState(frontObstacleDetected=true)
        System -> Drive: turnLeft90()
        note right of System: Return to original heading;\nremain stopped or evaluate additional backward movement.
    end
else backward unavailable
    note right of System: UC-003 confirmed front, left,\nand previous right direction are blocked.
    Sensor -> System: reportBackObstacleState(backObstacleDetected=true)
    activate System
    System -> Drive: stop()
end
deactivate System
@enduml
